File 5: pants-mapper.xq

This stays clean and small:

xquery version "3.1";

import module namespace tddm4 = "http://www.td.com/tddm-pacs004" at "tddm-pacs004-pdm-public.xq";
import module namespace tddm8 = "http://www.td.com/tddm-pacs008" at "tddm-pacs008-pdm-public.xq";
import module namespace tddm9 = "http://www.td.com/tddm-pacs009" at "tddm-pacs009-pdm-public.xq";

declare namespace output = "http://www.w3.org/2010/xslt-xquery-serialization";
declare option output:method "json";
declare option output:indent "yes";

declare variable $pdmPublic external;

let $jsonInput := parse-json($pdmPublic)
let $messageType := string($jsonInput?TDDMessage?TDDMessageBody?("x-type"))

return
  if ($messageType = "pacs.004") then
    tddm4:mapPacs004($jsonInput)
  else if ($messageType = "pacs.008") then
    tddm8:mapPacs008($jsonInput)
  else if ($messageType = "pacs.009") then
    tddm9:mapPacs009($jsonInput)
  else
    error(
      QName("http://www.td.com/errors", "UNKNOWN_MESSAGE_TYPE"),
      "Unknown message type: " || (($messageType, "<missing>")[1]),
      map { "received": (($messageType, "<missing>")[1]) }
    )
For your exact requirement of 20 common fields

You have 2 options.

Option A — common helper returns a base map

Best when those fields are identical across all pacs.

Example:

let $base := common:baseFields($jsonInput, "pacs.004")
return map:merge(($base, map { ...specific fields... }))

This is what I recommend.

Option B — common helper per section

Example:

common:customer($hvp)
common:posting($hvp)
common:agent(...)
common:id(...)

Best when some sections are reused but not always all 20 fields.

In practice, a mix of A and B is best.

One important improvement to your current helper

Your current safe-array-item is using 0-based style:

if ($idx ge 0 and $idx lt array:size($arr))

That is not ideal for the way you are calling fields semantically as 1, 2, 3.

Use 1-based indexing instead:

declare function common:safe-array-item($arr as item()*, $idx as xs:integer) as item()? {
  if (empty($arr)) then
    ()
  else if ($arr instance of array(*)) then
    if ($idx ge 1 and $idx le array:size($arr)) then
      $arr?($idx)
    else
      ()
  else if ($idx = 1) then
    $arr
  else
    ()
};

This matches:

address1 -> index 1
address2 -> index 2
address3 -> index 3

Much cleaner.

My recommendation

Do this:

Create pants-common.xq
Move:
normalizeOrNull
safe-array-item
all common field builders
into it
Keep pants-mapper.xq only as dispatcher
In each pacs file:
import pants-common.xq
build let $base := common:baseFields(...)
merge in pac-specific fields

That is the cleanest and most senior design.

